WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.288 --> 00:00:03.952
- She's an American soccer
player and Olympic gold medalist.

00:00:03.952 --> 00:00:06.616
She's a forward for the Portland Thorns FC

00:00:06.616 --> 00:00:09.088
and for the US Women's
National Soccer Team.

00:00:09.088 --> 00:00:12.193
She was the US Soccer
Female Athlete of the Year

00:00:12.193 --> 00:00:15.249
and a FIFA World Player
of the Year Finalist.

00:00:15.249 --> 00:00:16.501
She's Alex Morgan,

00:00:16.501 --> 00:00:20.001
and here are her top 10 rules for success.

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:24.078
- I played a lot of
sports when I was younger,

00:00:24.078 --> 00:00:25.574
and I was settled on soccer

00:00:25.574 --> 00:00:29.378
because the '99 team really motivated me.

00:00:29.378 --> 00:00:32.087
My dad would go out on the
soccer field with me every day

00:00:32.087 --> 00:00:33.651
and it pushed myself in a good way

00:00:33.651 --> 00:00:37.497
and motivated me to be the
best player I could be.

00:00:37.497 --> 00:00:38.650
Soccer was just my thing

00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:41.818
and I wanted to make it to
the US Women's National Team.

00:00:41.818 --> 00:00:45.043
("Titanium" by David Guetta featuring Sia)

00:00:45.043 --> 00:00:47.416
My favorite goal was against Italy.

00:00:47.416 --> 00:00:50.008
I scored in probably the 93rd minute,

00:00:50.008 --> 00:00:52.207
and I think that's one of the best parts

00:00:52.207 --> 00:00:54.457
of my game is my finishing.

00:00:57.001 --> 00:00:58.490
Everyone has their talent,

00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:02.670
but it's what you do with
that talent to make it great.

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:04.630
I'm not worried about my future,

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:07.069
about what I'm going to do
in 10 years after soccer.

00:01:07.069 --> 00:01:08.686
It's about right now,

00:01:08.686 --> 00:01:11.487
how I can contribute
to the team's success,

00:01:11.487 --> 00:01:14.482
how I can make sure that I'm physically

00:01:14.482 --> 00:01:16.109
and mentally ready for each game.

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:19.215
So, it's really just taking it day by day

00:01:19.215 --> 00:01:21.892
and knowing that the
future is so uncertain.

00:01:21.892 --> 00:01:23.931
You just need to be happy
where you are right now

00:01:23.931 --> 00:01:26.882
and just have a positive outlook on it.

00:01:26.882 --> 00:01:28.921
So, in the morning, I
get a good night's sleep,

00:01:28.921 --> 00:01:32.256
and in the mornings I try
and get out on here on Alki

00:01:32.256 --> 00:01:34.180
and just kind of walk around.

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:36.046
It's just a really beautiful place

00:01:36.046 --> 00:01:37.358
to kind of start your morning

00:01:37.358 --> 00:01:41.525
and have a positive mentality
going into your day.

00:01:42.494 --> 00:01:45.089
Yoga definitely fits into my life

00:01:45.089 --> 00:01:46.286
in terms of preparation.

00:01:46.286 --> 00:01:48.319
It's great just to have that sense

00:01:48.319 --> 00:01:50.434
of feeling at ease with yourself.

00:01:50.434 --> 00:01:52.263
Stretching is a huge part of soccer

00:01:52.263 --> 00:01:55.041
and making sure that
you're pretty flexible,

00:01:55.041 --> 00:01:56.299
and I just love the feeling

00:01:56.299 --> 00:01:58.251
of kind of being alone a little bit

00:01:58.251 --> 00:02:01.373
and being able to take
my mind off of soccer,

00:02:01.373 --> 00:02:03.514
but at the same time, the
reason I go to yoga is

00:02:03.514 --> 00:02:06.182
to help me succeed in soccer.

00:02:06.182 --> 00:02:07.990
I didn't expect when I sprained my ankle

00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:11.756
back in late October that
it would come to this,

00:02:11.756 --> 00:02:13.373
and that was the hardest part for me,

00:02:13.373 --> 00:02:14.854
was kind of doubting myself,

00:02:14.854 --> 00:02:18.536
like, well, why didn't I take it easier?

00:02:18.536 --> 00:02:20.553
Why didn't I kind of pull
myself out of training

00:02:20.553 --> 00:02:21.859
or out of a game?

00:02:21.859 --> 00:02:23.927
But you can't look back.

00:02:23.927 --> 00:02:25.974
You kind of just need to look forward.

00:02:25.974 --> 00:02:28.805
It was definitely hard,
but I feel like now

00:02:28.805 --> 00:02:30.660
that I'm actually seeing improvement.

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:32.110
We just got an MRI.

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:34.377
It kind of helps me a little bit mentally

00:02:34.377 --> 00:02:37.656
to be able to do a bike a
little bit, to be able to swim.

00:02:37.656 --> 00:02:39.265
I wasn't able to do anything on crutches,

00:02:39.265 --> 00:02:41.834
so now knowing that there's improvement,

00:02:41.834 --> 00:02:43.161
I'm able to do some stuff,

00:02:43.161 --> 00:02:45.994
I feel a lot more, I guess, happy.

00:02:47.346 --> 00:02:51.732
Before every game, the key to
my preparation is consistency.

00:02:51.732 --> 00:02:53.496
I really think that every athlete

00:02:53.496 --> 00:02:55.612
is a little bit superstitious,

00:02:55.612 --> 00:02:57.227
and if an athlete tells you otherwise,

00:02:57.227 --> 00:02:58.516
I think they're lying.

00:02:58.516 --> 00:03:00.544
So, yes, I do a couple of things.

00:03:00.544 --> 00:03:03.319
I definitely put on my right
sock before my left sock,

00:03:03.319 --> 00:03:05.219
and I like to take a nap at the same time

00:03:05.219 --> 00:03:07.026
and eat the same things,

00:03:07.026 --> 00:03:08.308
and then right before the game I like

00:03:08.308 --> 00:03:10.030
to do a lot of mental visualization,

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:13.307
so I'll go in a locker
and just put on headphones

00:03:13.307 --> 00:03:15.707
and just imagine myself in the game.

00:03:15.707 --> 00:03:19.175
When people ask me how I
balance non-soccer stuff,

00:03:19.175 --> 00:03:22.627
the things off the field, I think it just,

00:03:22.627 --> 00:03:25.262
I've been more confident
in the last couple of years

00:03:25.262 --> 00:03:26.651
with the decisions I make

00:03:26.651 --> 00:03:27.856
and the opportunities that I'm given

00:03:27.856 --> 00:03:31.569
and the decisions whether to
go through with it or not.

00:03:31.569 --> 00:03:34.009
If it's authentic to who I am,

00:03:34.009 --> 00:03:35.696
whether it's a company I'm representing

00:03:35.696 --> 00:03:37.125
or whether it's an event I'm going to

00:03:37.125 --> 00:03:40.563
or whether it's a photo shoot
that I've been asked to do,

00:03:40.563 --> 00:03:43.157
I think it's just
weighing all of the things

00:03:43.157 --> 00:03:44.878
and making sure that nothing is standing

00:03:44.878 --> 00:03:47.684
in the way of what I do
best and what I'm here for,

00:03:47.684 --> 00:03:50.026
and that's to play soccer.

00:03:50.026 --> 00:03:52.502
I think there's no secret to success.

00:03:52.502 --> 00:03:55.712
I mean, I think Abby definitely
hit the nail on the head.

00:03:55.712 --> 00:03:57.422
It's all about hard work.

00:03:57.422 --> 00:03:58.738
It's all about going out there

00:03:58.738 --> 00:04:02.148
and practicing more than your opponent,

00:04:02.148 --> 00:04:02.981
than your teammates.

00:04:02.981 --> 00:04:06.020
It's about mentally
preparing every single day.

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:10.708
It's about not slacking off,
putting in that time and work.

00:04:10.708 --> 00:04:14.875
And you can tell from Abby
that she has put in that work,

00:04:15.982 --> 00:04:20.157
and that's, I think, the reason
that she is so successful.

00:04:20.157 --> 00:04:23.907
But at the end of the
day, there is no secret

00:04:24.836 --> 00:04:27.169
to why we are so successful.

00:04:28.371 --> 00:04:31.608
I think most forwards like
to play under pressure,

00:04:31.608 --> 00:04:35.013
or else you wouldn't play
the forward position.

00:04:35.013 --> 00:04:37.441
But I do like that pressure.

00:04:37.441 --> 00:04:42.105
And sometimes you don't always
succeed, and that's okay.

00:04:42.105 --> 00:04:45.461
And as a forward you have
to find that balance.

00:04:45.461 --> 00:04:47.109
I mean, you're going to shoot five times

00:04:47.109 --> 00:04:49.841
and maybe you'll score
once, maybe you won't.

00:04:49.841 --> 00:04:51.560
Maybe you'll get three
goals out of three shots.

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:53.649
So, it's a little unpredictable

00:04:53.649 --> 00:04:56.140
and you've just kind of got to go with it

00:04:56.140 --> 00:04:58.262
and have confidence in yourself.

00:04:58.262 --> 00:05:02.221
You know, I've wanted to
be an Olympic gold medalist

00:05:02.221 --> 00:05:05.294
since I was seven years old,

00:05:05.294 --> 00:05:07.792
so that was a dream come true for me.

00:05:07.792 --> 00:05:09.415
- Your role models are who, I wonder?

00:05:09.415 --> 00:05:11.186
- My role models, I mean,
I definitely looked up

00:05:11.186 --> 00:05:14.795
to Kristine Lilly, Mia Hamm,
Abby even in high school

00:05:14.795 --> 00:05:16.294
and getting on the national team.

00:05:16.294 --> 00:05:17.793
But I feel like I always wanted

00:05:17.793 --> 00:05:19.174
to kind of make my parents proud,

00:05:19.174 --> 00:05:20.502
and they were the two people

00:05:20.502 --> 00:05:21.947
that came to every single game

00:05:21.947 --> 00:05:24.447
and just were my biggest fans.

00:05:25.369 --> 00:05:26.853
It's not what I wanted them to see.

00:05:26.853 --> 00:05:28.868
I just wanted them to feel the passion

00:05:28.868 --> 00:05:31.329
and I wanted them to grow that passion,

00:05:31.329 --> 00:05:34.115
because this is exactly what I dreamed of

00:05:34.115 --> 00:05:36.344
when I was a young kid,
when I was watching you.

00:05:36.344 --> 00:05:38.462
This is what I dreamed off.

00:05:38.462 --> 00:05:39.629
I'm going to cry.

00:05:40.721 --> 00:05:43.535
- [Interviewer] You're
going to make me cry; stop.

00:05:43.535 --> 00:05:48.093
- But just to dream big,
'cause dreams do happen.

00:05:48.093 --> 00:05:49.455
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:05:49.455 --> 00:05:52.689
I made this video because
Zephrin Pinto asked me to

00:05:52.689 --> 00:05:54.139
for his daughter.

00:05:54.139 --> 00:05:55.710
So, if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:57.448
that you want me to profile next,

00:05:57.448 --> 00:06:00.171
leave it in the comments below
and I'll see what I can do.

00:06:00.171 --> 00:06:01.243
I'd also love to know which

00:06:01.243 --> 00:06:04.350
of Alex Morgan's top 10
rules you like the best.

00:06:04.350 --> 00:06:05.226
Leave it in the comments.

00:06:05.226 --> 00:06:07.021
I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:06:07.021 --> 00:06:08.625
Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:06:08.625 --> 00:06:12.208
Continue to believe,
and I'll see you soon.

